###############################################################################
# MIS PoC — requirement tests (VS Code "REST Client" / JetBrains HTTP client)
#
# Prereq:  cd mis-dev && make infra-up      (Kong on :8000)
#          then run the services — host:  make dev s=auth / s=case
#                                  or:     make stack-up   (after make images-build)
#
# Run requests top-to-bottom: the login calls are @named and later requests
# reuse their captured tokens. Expected status is noted on each request.
###############################################################################

@gateway   = http://localhost:8000
@authDirect = http://localhost:3001

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. WHITELISTED ENDPOINTS  (no token required — Kong <svc>-public routes)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### auth health — expect 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/health

### case health — expect 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/health

### case ready — expect 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/ready

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. PROTECTED WITHOUT A TOKEN  (Kong jwt rejects at the edge — expect 401)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### case root, no token — expect 401
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/

### /me with no token — expect 401 (introspection still needs a valid token)
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/me

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. LOGIN  (whitelisted /api/auth/login — issues the JWT Kong will accept)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Login as CASE OFFICER (by username) — expect 200
# @name loginCase
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "usernameOrEmail": "caseofficer", "password": "case123" }

###
@caseToken = {{loginCase.response.body.access_token}}

### Login as REPORTING ANALYST (by email) — expect 200
# @name loginReport
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "usernameOrEmail": "report.analyst@mis.local", "password": "report123" }

###
@reportToken = {{loginReport.response.body.access_token}}

### Login with bad credentials — expect 401
POST {{gateway}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "usernameOrEmail": "caseofficer", "password": "wrong" }

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. AUTHORIZATION MATRIX  (case-officer vs reporting-analyst)
#    Requirement: a user without the service's required permission is denied.
#    case-officer has case:read; reporting-analyst does NOT.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### case-officer  ->  CASE service   — expect 200 (has case:read)
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/
Authorization: Bearer {{caseToken}}

### reporting-analyst  ->  CASE service — expect 403 (lacks case:read)
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/
Authorization: Bearer {{reportToken}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. /me — current user's roles & resolved permissions (any service)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### case-officer introspects on the CASE service — expect 200, role case-officer
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/me
Authorization: Bearer {{caseToken}}

### reporting-analyst introspects on the AUTH service — expect 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{reportToken}}

### cross-service introspection is allowed (still token-gated) — expect 200
GET {{gateway}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{caseToken}}

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. GATEWAY CROSS-CUTTING  (correlation id, metrics, rate limiting)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Correlation id: response echoes X-Correlation-ID (generated by Kong)
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/health

### Client-supplied correlation id passes through unchanged
GET {{gateway}}/api/cases/health
X-Correlation-ID: my-trace-abc-123

### Kong Prometheus metrics (status listener) — expect 200, text exposition
GET http://localhost:8100/metrics

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 7. DIRECT TO SERVICE (bypasses Kong — no auth enforced by Kong, but the
#    in-service accessGuard still applies for non-whitelisted paths)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Direct health (no Kong) — expect 200
GET {{authDirect}}/api/auth/health

### Direct login (no Kong) — expect 200
POST {{authDirect}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "usernameOrEmail": "caseofficer", "password": "case123" }
